This repository includes Battle Drones, a browser strategy game.

  Name:    Battle Drones
  Authors: Simon Willison, Eli Albert, and commits authored by Claude
           (Anthropic), per the upstream git history
  Source:  https://github.com/simonw/battledrones
  Commit:  ca4f13b36013e1980289046e731a295d2bf02a3e
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Path:    games/battledrones/

Upstream carries no copyright line of its own and no NOTICE file. The game's
license is kept unchanged at games/battledrones/LICENSE.

Changes to the upstream tree: progress-shots/, research_notes/ and
package-lock.json are removed, and package.json gains the check, stage and
deploy scripts. Later changes are in this repository's git history.

The images the game ships were generated with an image model, except the HUD
portraits, which are renders of the game's 3D models (see
games/battledrones/ART.md).

This repository includes Tree Appreciator, a browser spot-the-difference game.

  Name:    Tree Appreciator
  Authors: Simon Willison, generated with Claude Opus 5.5, per the upstream
           commit message
  Source:  https://github.com/simonw/tools
  Commit:  dafb677a5d54a89c32a80d1c9b6a7ab7318d55c3
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Path:    games/tree-appreciator/

The upstream file tree-appreciator.html is imported unchanged as
games/tree-appreciator/index.html. The license of simonw/tools is kept at
games/tree-appreciator/LICENSE. The game loads three.js r128 from cdnjs and
its fonts from Google Fonts at run time.

This repository includes Emberwick, a browser adventure game.

  Name:    Emberwick
  Authors: Simon Willison
  Source:  https://simonw.github.io/emberwick/v11/emberwick.html and the
           files under https://simonw.github.io/emberwick/v11/src/
  Fetched: 2026-11-25
  SHA-256: 86d2fefc44cc82ca411d98da8ec44d4dec61af5a595f7619de90cc296951bbef
           (emberwick.html)
  License: none. Upstream publishes no license; all rights are reserved by
           the author.
  Path:    games/emberwick/

The repository owner imported Emberwick without a license and accepts that
risk. It will be removed if the author objects. games/emberwick/src/ holds the
upstream source files unchanged. games/emberwick/shell.html is the published
page with its module script replaced by a marker, and build.ts rebuilds the
page from the two. The one change to the upstream files is a
<meta charset="utf-8"> line added to shell.html. The game loads three.js 0.170.0 from jsDelivr and its fonts
from Google Fonts at run time.

